{
  "id": "u1kre",
  "title": "PostgreSQL Average Active Sessions Dashboard in VS Code",
  "published_at": "2026-06-11",
  "canonical_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/postgresql-average-active-sessions-dashboard-vs-code-franck-pachot-u1kre",
  "author": "Franck Pachot",
  "body_html": "\n<!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">Troubleshooting database performance often starts with a simple question: </span><span class=\"italic\">what are your sessions waiting on?</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">You can install the </span><span class=\"\"><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmarketplace%2Evisualstudio%2Ecom%2Fitems%3FitemName%3Dms-ossdata%2Evscode-pgsql&amp;urlhash=oG5F&amp;trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block\" target=\"_blank\" data-tracking-control-name=\"article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block\" data-tracking-will-navigate=\"\" data-test-link=\"\">PostgreSQL extension for Visual Studio Code<!----></a></span><span class=\"\"> and connect to your database in minutes. With one more click, you get quick insight into overall performance—such as how many sessions are active or waiting. This helps you verify whether it matches your expectations based on your connection pool, database size, and workload.</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">For example, the default pgbench workload stresses row locks because all sessions update the same row. With 10 clients (pgbench -c 10), you can expect about 10 active sessions, most of them waiting to acquire a lock. You can see this in pg_stat_activity, where each session appears as a row with its state and wait event. A graphical view makes this much easier to understand. This is what you can see in VS Code or any compatible IDE that supports VS Code extensions (such as Kiro or Cursor):</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQHzYn460YrKEw/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ6zU02xHoAM-/0/1781125042260?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=xL3ki4vASOd3VvcmzIl8vu2N-pqx_Bghym1jdF_B4pQ\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Microsoft VS Code extension for PostgreSQL ➤ Performance Dashboard ➤ Waits</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">To get this view, install the Microsoft PostgreSQL extension for VS Code:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQGZHIJXkLxiUA/article-inline_image-shrink_1500_2232/B4EZ6zVtd0JIAY-/0/1781125273749?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=jLTHomXE5jt2lPgzwjXGTdm03eBV9PUYkkzURTpp0fA\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-pgsql/blob/main/README.md</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">Define a new connection with your authentication and server details:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQHh-hWtDefjZw/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ6zWlAJIMAM-/0/1781125501276?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=sqAIINxs5dfWDxeeuuBmE91t_nDMrvzZvqo7oDFANBA\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Connections  ➤ Add new connection</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">Right-click the connection and select </span><span class=\"font-[700]\">Dashboard</span><span class=\"\">:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQFbYXE88BzXTw/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ6zWRVJHMAM-/0/1781125420666?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=RGqht9OUphgBCVcVQZC27mihHWpZXfQD6wQsVFNuDAs\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Connection  ➤ Dashboard</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">The </span><span class=\"font-[700]\">Readiness</span><span class=\"\"> section recommends enabling track_io_timing, track_wal_io_timing, and installing pg_stat_statements. These are required to view top SQL history, but not for the active session visualization.</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">The active session timeline is refreshed every 10 seconds. The X-axis represents time, and the Y-axis shows the number of active sessions by wait type.</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">Here is an example where 47 session backends are waiting on a lock, 1 is waiting on I/O, and 1 is running on CPU:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQFT5jK81u1i7w/article-inline_image-shrink_1000_1488/B4EZ6zYFqxKsAI-/0/1781125897174?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=DreLxgJOMBWT1YgYgEIGrVhzGAbT8TKbgDqwufq18Jk\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Dashboard ➤ Waits for pgbench -c 50  -b tcpb-like</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">Those are wait types, the wait event detail is available in a </span><span class=\"font-[700]\">Wait Events Ranked</span><span class=\"\"> section:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQHip31mJTRlKQ/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ61oTu1HkAQ-/0/1781163703515?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=q5EnXiT2Saq3MiBFNxw1ijPT2TWHE7-y53SAQh0u1XI\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Dashboard ➤ Wait events for pgbench -b tcpb-like</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">The </span><span class=\"font-[700]\">Sessions</span><span class=\"\"> tab shows additional metrics that help explain the locking behind those waits. In this case, no single session is blocking all others—the number of blocked and blocking sessions is similar:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQGoShwWSzG5Nw/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ6zYsPwIMAQ-/0/1781126055528?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=go5h3VFFtw_Do0XNMCupzeykXQyzUkfNG6SKBoHoW9E\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Dashboard ➤ Server Metrics for pgbench -c 50</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">The session table queries pg_stat_activity to show those sessions, so you can identify where they come from and which queries are responsible for the waits:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n\n    \n      <div class=\"flex flex-col mt-2\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block\" rel=\"ugc\">\n        \n      <figure>\n        <img alt=\"Article content\" class=\"lazy-load block w-full\" data-delayed-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E12AQEsvzuNfR72Dg/article-inline_image-shrink_400_744/B4EZ6zZd1zIMAM-/0/1781126258429?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=Lnh0QBwBJr4IuxzA2eXPeWJDOpeu9FPvMKvL3rB2OfQ\">\n          <figcaption class=\"mt-[0.8rem] text-center text-sm font-normal text-color-text-low-emphasis\" data-test-id=\"publishing-image-block-caption\">\n            <span class=\"\">Dashboard ➤ Sessions Table for pgbench -c 50</span><!---->\n          </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    \n      </div>\n  \n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">This makes it easy to validate workload behavior and quickly diagnose contention issues—without leaving your development environment. The PostgreSQL extension for VS Code includes many features that help developers interact with their database directly from the IDE:</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n    \n    <div data-test-id=\"publishing-embed-block\" class=\"mt-4 pulse-publishing-embed-block invisible\">\n      <iframe allowfullscreen=\"\" frameborder=\"0\" class=\"publishing-embed-block-iframe max-w-full \" height=\"405\" width=\"720\" src=\"https://www.linkedin.com/embeds/publishingEmbed.html?articleId=7212030440253085132\" title=\"Announcing a new IDE for PostgreSQL in VS Code from Microsoft | Microsoft Community Hub\">\n      </iframe>\n    </div>\n  \n<!----><!---->                  \n\n    <div class=\"article-main__content\" data-test-id=\"publishing-text-block\">\n        <p>\n          <span class=\"\">I’d love to hear your feedback—what works well, and what could be improved? Anything that can improve the developer experience with PostgreSQL is worth exploring.</span><!---->\n        </p>\n    </div>\n  \n<!---->              ",
  "tags": []
}
